+\subsubsection{Independent calibration and falsification gates}
+
+For every alpha-blind calibration configuration define
+\begin{align}
+    y_n
+    &:=
+    \mathscr R_{\rm micro}
+    [\gamma_n,f_n,\Omega_{3,n}]
+    -
+    \frac{8\pi}{3}\mathcal L_{D,n}
+    \nonumber\\
+    &=
+    \sum_a A_{na}c_a+\varepsilon_n.
+    \label{eq:rt_alpha_calibration_equation_v0835}
+\end{align}
+The minimal campaign is:
+\begin{enumerate}
+    \item circular finite-core rings at several \(R/D\), isolating bend;
+    \item straight periodic materially twisted tubes, isolating twist;
+    \item antiparallel finite-core tube pairs at several separations,
+    isolating contact;
+    \item mixed twisted, curved, and near-contact geometries retained as
+    holdouts;
+    \item cross-representation and cross-knot predictions using one frozen
+    coefficient vector;
+    \item one final trefoil comparison at a preregistered tolerance.
+\end{enumerate}
+The target \(\alpha\), the final correction, the elementary charge, and a
+swirl speed already calibrated through \(\alpha\) are forbidden inputs.
+Promotion requires full-rank identifiability, regulator and resolution
+convergence, acceptable residuals, leave-one-out success, mixed holdout
+success, and no coefficient change after the trefoil geometry is opened.
+
+\paragraph{Current verdict.}
+The projector identity, radius--diameter conversion, tube-volume no-go,
+Euler--Biot--Savart formula, and twist-energy lower bound are derived under
+their declared hypotheses.  The Wilson coefficients and electromagnetic
+matching remain open.  Neither
+\(\Delta_{3_1}^{\rm HR}\) nor
+\(\Delta_{3_1}^{\rm Gilbert}\) is presently an independent SST prediction.
